---
/**
 * /roadmap/ — renders the public roadmap at build time.
 *
 * WHY NOT ROADMAP.md
 * It used to render that file, and the result was neither safe nor readable.
 * The internal roadmap stacks three plans — the active one and two superseded
 * ones — and carries build budgets, asset vendors, tool costs and source paths.
 * A visitor met "Legacy Unity roadmap — superseded" next to a phase priced in
 * credits, with nothing to indicate which plan was current.
 *
 * content/roadmap.md is written for players: what works now, what is being
 * built, what is only an intention, and what is deliberately not planned. The
 * internal roadmap stays internal.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DocToc from "../components/DocToc.astro";
import { renderDoc } from "../lib/markdown";

const { html, headings } = renderDoc("content/roadmap.md");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Roadmap"
  pathname="/roadmap/"
  description="What's built, what's next, and the order Isoperia's 3D open-world rebuild is being tackled in."
>
  <section class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="doc__intro" data-reveal>
        <h1>Roadmap</h1>
        <p>
          Where Isoperia is going, in the order it is being tackled. There are no dates on
          it and nothing here is a commitment — the ordering is the useful part, and it
          changes as the game does.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="doc-grid">
        <DocToc headings={headings} label="Roadmap sections" />

        <div class="prose" set:html={html} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Page-local only. The shared .prose, .toc, .table-wrap and .doc-grid rules
     live in src/styles/components.css — this file must not restate them, or the
     two drift and a change in one place stops taking effect. */
  .doc {
    padding-block: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .doc__intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .doc__intro p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
